{
  "_about": [
    "Controlled vocabulary for the Idlib FTTH project.",
    "",
    "'terms' defines the canonical concepts: an ASCII code that machines group by,",
    "and the Arabic label that people read. Arabic is the display language; the code",
    "is never shown to a user.",
    "",
    "'aliases' maps every raw string found in the source shapefiles onto a code.",
    "The raw string is ALSO stored verbatim in <table>.type_raw, so nothing is lost",
    "and a wrong mapping is a config edit rather than a data migration.",
    "",
    "To add a term: add it to 'terms', then map its raw spellings in 'aliases',",
    "then re-run tools/build_geopackage.py. Unmapped raw values are not guessed -",
    "they land with a NULL code and are listed by the v_qa_vocab view."
  ],

